# Generated identity ledger + its receipt, both written by
# tools/scripts/gpu_handoff_provenance.py. The receipt is what collides
# unconditionally: source_commit and the handoff_sha256 over the whole ledger
# move on every regeneration, whatever else did. The ledger itself is milder,
# because a row is pinned to the commit that last touched its own path, so a
# main move re-pins only the rows whose paths it touched.
# The version bot's bump commit carries the re-pin on main
# (version_at_land._refresh_derived), so a branch does not regenerate these:
# gpu_handoff_pin_freshness.py rejects an identity-only refresh at push. When
# the driver is installed it resolves what it can to a deliberately invalid
# value that gates.sh rejects; the repair is to restore the base's copy with
# `git checkout <base> -- <paths>`, not to regenerate, which would land in that
# guard. An editorial edit to the ledger is still a legitimate in-PR change and
# still owes `gpu_handoff_provenance.py write --receipt`. Install the driver
# with setup.sh (or tools/scripts/install-githooks.sh); a checkout without it
# gets today's text conflict, which is the status quo rather than a worse
# outcome.
docs/status/gpu-vellum-handoff.yaml merge=pulp-gpu-ledger
docs/validation/gpu-handoff-provenance/receipt.json merge=pulp-gpu-ledger
